arm64-darwin  cxx1 guards the allocation in `new Derived` and `new Base` since 2026-09-26 - [expr.new]/20, the storage freed if the constructor throws - so it emits the cleanup pad's __Unwind_Resume; Darwin's clang emits no cleanup for those allocations, though Linux's does for the same shape, and on x86_64-linux the two now agree on every name. The other 22 names agree here.
